+++ b/docs/development/ADRs/next/0028-Scan_Input_Fusion.md
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+# Scan-input fusion before DaCe lowering
+
+Status: experimental, opt-in.
+
+## Context
+
+ICON's vertical forward sweep materializes coefficient fields before consuming
+them in a scan. Moving arithmetic into the model scan removes those arrays but
+mixes compiler concerns with scientific equations. Existing `FuseAsFieldOp` can
+inline scan inputs, but DaCe scan lowering expects scalar values at the current
+level and cannot directly lower the shifted iterators introduced by that fusion.
+
+## Decision
+
+Add the backend option `optimization_args={"fuse_scan_inputs": True}` (default
+False). The DaCe translator consumes this option before building the SDFG;
+remaining options still reach `gt_auto_optimize`. It applies existing field-op
+fusion to scan-containing assignments and represents fixed vertical shifts as
+separate shifted field inputs. Unsupported shifted accesses retain the original
+assignment. The transformation does not change scan direction or initial state.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Applications can configure the option through their existing backend settings
+without rewriting model equations. The option participates in translation
+configuration/caching and is independent of the SDFG hook interface. It is not
+an SDFG pass and must not be invoked from `TopLevelDataFlowStep`. CPU correctness
+and generated storage must be checked before GPU performance is claimed. The
+measured model-code implementation remains the comparison reference until the
+compiler route is validated on the GPU granule.
